  "_comment": "Server-side screen on top of dec6 (lease, 8 slots on the shared pool, at most 6 new-task decodes, KV budget 24,576). Same scheduler args in every run; only llama-server flags change. Why: on lease_kvu8_c6 0.95X/1.15X seed 42, 18-21% of decode time overlaps another slot's prompt prefill, and each overlapped second costs ~0.76 s (analysis.prefill_stall), mostly first-step prompts (median ~1.6K tokens) processed in one 2,048-token batch. dec6_b512 / dec6_b256 cap the tokens per server step (-b/-ub) so decoding slots get a token after every 512 / 256 prompt tokens (chunked prefill); expect less decode stall, somewhat slower prefill and TTFT. dec6_q8 stores K and V as q8_0 (flash attention forced on, which auto already picks on the 3080): decode reads about half the KV bytes per token; the pool size (CTX 24,576) is kept the same so only the speed changes. Seed 42 at 0.95X and 1.15X, 8 runs, ~2.4 h. A screen, not a result. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_srv_quick --baseline lease_kvu8_dec6; and python -m analysis.prefill_stall on each run.",
